// IsolationHolders.mo - WHO MAY SEND EACH ACT, restated by the isolation battery in its own file.
//
// The gate's table (`Gate.HOLDERS`) is what the contract enforces; this is what the battery holds it to. They are
// two tables on purpose: the probe in Isolation.test.mo takes its expectations from THIS one, so a family whose
// holders are widened in the gate - a role added, a role-held act made any member's, a member's act made a
// visitor's - is a family the probe sends from a principal the battery says must be refused, and the battery goes
// red. A change of policy is a change to both, made in the open; a change to one is a fault.
//
// The policy, by family:
//   #founder    bringing a company into existence: anyone, and the caller becomes its first administrator
//   #claim      the platform operator's claim: only while no operator is named and no company exists
//   #platform   the platform operator's acts, the statutory schedules every company's payroll reads among them
//   #offered    accepting the platform operator's role: only the principal the standing offer names
//   #uploader   a chunk, a seal or an abort of an upload: only the member who began it
//   #visitor    the acts a member of the public sends to a company that exists, held by their folds to the
//               visitor's own cart, conversation, application or offer, or to a device's verified signature
//   #member     any member in standing but the company's auditor, who holds no act
//   #roles      a member in standing holding one of the roles named
//   #self       the member the act is about, or a member holding one of the roles named
//
// Attribution: Thebes Core Team. Licence: Apache 2.0.

import Gate "../src/Gate";

